	affiliations = {Department of Computing and Information Sciences, University of Technology and Applied Sciences, Muscat, Oman},
	abstract = {Landslides and sandstorms pose significant risks to infrastructure and human safety across arid regions such as Oman and the wider GCC, where rapid environmental changes intensify hazard frequency and impact. This paper presents an Artificial Intelligence and Internet of Things (AI–IoT)–based Federated Edge and Digital Twin Framework designed for real-time landslide and sandstorm forecasting with climate-resilient early warning. The proposed architecture integrates Federated Edge Intelligence, TinyML-powered edge nodes, and Digital Twin modeling to enable decentralized, privacy-preserving, and low-latency hazard prediction. A network of heterogeneous sensors—including LiDAR, hyperspectral particulate sensors, MEMS accelerometers, and soil-moisture probes—collects continuous geotechnical and atmospheric data from high-risk zones. Edge nodes perform on-site anomaly detection and transmit aggregated insights to a cloud-based Digital Twin, which fuses satellite SAR imagery, geospatial models, and real-time sensor data to simulate terrain dynamics and environmental stress responses. The system employs LoRaWAN and 5G URLLC for reliable long-range and ultra-low-latency communication, while wearable haptic alert devices ensure localized and multilingual notifications even in connectivity-challenged areas. A reinforcement learning–driven alert prioritization engine minimizes false alarms and enhances situational accuracy. By combining AI-driven sensing, federated learning, immersive geospatial visualization, and adaptive early-warning mechanisms, the framework advances disaster readiness, safeguards human life and infrastructure, and aligns with sustainable climate adaptation goals for arid and semi-arid ecosystems. The framework was validated through simulation and field datasets demonstrating 94.8% accuracy and sub-3second latency, with containerized scalability and federated privacy protection ensuring real-world deployability. © 2025 IEEE.},
