	abstract = {Industrial automation with Internet of Things(IIoT) systems in critical water treatment infrastructure face escalating cybersecurity risks that target the cyber-physical layer. The detrimental latency is introduced and a single point of failure is presented using the Traditional cloud-centric anomaly architectures. This study proposes an edge centric security approach in which Tiny Machine Learning model (TinyML) has been deployed directly on edge device ESP32 based sensors to perform anomaly detection effectively at the data source. This proposed system maintains a bidirectional connection with the Innovate Engineering Products IoT (IEP-IoT) platform for visualization, historical monitoring and alert handling, enabling coordinate edge cloud operation validation using the BATADAL water treatment SCADA data set, shows that the proposed framework detects complex attacks such as pressure tampering, water flow manipulation and unauthorized control commands compared with conventional threshold based methods. This framework achieves approximately a 23 % improvement in deduction performance while reducing cloud data transmission by over 85 % by executing inference locally. The system minimizes energy consumption and latency making it suitable for resource constraint safety critical industrial environments. © 2026 IEEE.},
