	affiliations = {St. Joseph's College of Engineering Omr, Dept of Ece, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {LPG finds widespread application in both domestic and industrial fields. However, accidental leakage and/or unreliable control of gas levels result in serious safety and economic hazards. To address this issue, this work discusses an intelligent LPG tracking and safety system using sensor technology integrated with AI. The developed system utilizes a load cell sensor to continuously measure gas level, always detecting leakage; it uses AI algorithms like TinyML-based MLP for prediction of gas consumption behavior and Random Forest for anomaly detection in usage behavior. Graced with prediction and diagnostic capabilities, the proposed approach enables timely alerts and prevention through IoT-based notifications, thus minimizing the probability of explosions, shortages, and wastage. In addition, the system is able to automate booking upon the detection of low levels in the gas cylinders so that there will be a continuous supply without disruption. The major technical contribution of this work is a low-cost, adaptive AI framework that learns user-specific usage patterns and improves safety, while scaling to an efficient solution suitable for both domestic and industrial scenarios.  © 2025 IEEE.},
