	affiliations = {R G M College of Engineering and Technology, Andhra pradesh, India},
	abstract = {Low-cost environmental sensors are widely used in Internet of Things (IoT) systems; however, their reliability degrades over time due to gradual sensor drift. Detecting such drift is challenging using traditional threshold-based methods, especially when changes occur slowly. This paper proposes a lightweight edge-based approach for real-time sensor drift detection using supervised machine learning. Temperature and humidity data collected from a DHT11 sensor are processed using statistical feature extraction techniques, and multiple classification algorithms are evaluated. The selected Decision Tree model is deployed directly on an ESP8266 microcontroller, enabling real-time local inference without cloud dependency. The model achieved 96.8% accuracy with low inference latency (18 ms), demonstrating its effectiveness and feasibility for real-time edge deployment. The results highlight the potential of lightweight machine learning models for improving sensor reliability in IoT applications. © 2026 IEEE.},
