	abstract = {Leaks of refrigerant from automotive air conditioning systems endanger performance and represent a hazard to environmental safety and human health. This challenge is often a difficult condition to identify early, which can cause engine damage, health hazards and even flammable condition that might bring the fire. An early stage leak detection strategy can be introduced to the industry through implementation of the Tiny Machine Learning (TinyML) and IoT sensors, allowing the Predictive Maintenance strategy to be deployed. Real time anomaly detection: It monitors the system and gives proactive maintenance through pressure, temperature & gas leak sensors and TinyML. This approach also provides a reliable system, increases the system reliability, and decreases repair costs when the issues are identified and fixed before they have become costly to repair. To implement this IoT sensors are installed at different places in AC system, these IoT sensors are integrated with a TinyML model to analyze on the data gathered, making a system in real time to alert the error so that timely action can be taken. The AC performance is guaranteed at best level, the lifetime of the automotive air conditioning system is secured and the safety is improved. Tiny Machine Learning (TinyML) and Internet of Things (IoT) together forms a very disruptive solution for the predictive maintenance and real time decision support in automotive air conditioning (AC) systems. It is possible to use TinyML algorithms to run in realtime on these sensors to recognize anomalies of the system parameters such as pressure, temperature, and refrigerant levels etc. and other major incidents such as refrigerant leakages, temperature variations, and system inefficiencies at the earliest. By using the proactive strategy, the reliability and performance of automotive AC systems are improved, safety is increased, repair costs are decreased, the regulations for the environment are adhere to, the system life