	abstract = {Poultry farming faces persistent challenges in maintaining optimal environmental conditions and ensuring bird health, often leading to productivity losses due to delayed detection of abnormal situations. This paper presents an AIoT-based Anomaly Detection and Monitoring System for Smart Poultry Farms that integrates Internet of Things sensing with artificial intelligence to enable real-time monitoring and automated control. Environmental parameters including temperature, humidity, and ammonia concentration are continuously collected using IoT sensors and transmitted to a cloud platform. A lightweight 1D-CNN Autoencoder model is employed to learn normal multivariate sensor patterns and identify anomalies based on reconstruction error without requiring labeled data. The proposed system also supports automated actuation of ventilation, water spraying, and heating mechanisms, along with mobile-based alerts and visualization. Experimental validation was conducted using 30 days of real sensor data, comprising approximately 18,000 sequences, collected from a prototype poultry setup. The system achieved over 96% anomaly detection accuracy and reduced average response time from 18.2 s to 5.5 s while improving energy utilization efficiency from 72.3% to 88.5%. These results demonstrate the effectiveness of integrating AI and IoT for early anomaly detection, reduced manual intervention, and improved environmental stability, contributing toward sustainable and intelligent poultry farm management.  © 2026 IEEE.},
