	abstract = {This paper presents the design and validation of an IIoT-enabled AC-DC power supply integrating a multi-model embedded machine learning framework for secure, real-time fault detection in the oil and gas industry. Unlike conventional PC-based, single-model, or cloud-dependent approaches, the proposed architecture executes multiple lightweight classifiers directly on a microcontroller, achieving bounded, sub-millisecond inference while operating within strict speed and memory constraints. Runtime intelligence enables adaptive model selection and early-exit logic, while secure dual-path remote telemetry via HTTPS/TLS and local Modbus RTU ensures continuous SCADA integration in EMI-prone, intermittently connected environments. Experimental validation on a custom industrial-grade prototype achieved up to 97.47% accuracy with a macro F1-score of 0.96 across seven fault categories. At a 480 MHz clock, inference latencies are as low as 0.001 ms for the Decision Tree and 0.02 ms for the Quantized Neural Network, with less than 50 kB additional Flash memory. These results confirm the framework's suitability as a field-ready, extensible solution for embedding intelligent, resilient fault detection directly into industrial power conversion systems operating in remote, harsh environments. © 1972-2012 IEEE.},
