	year = {2026},
	journal = {2026 International Conference on Data Science, Agents and Artificial Intelligence, ICDSAAI 2026},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ICDSAAI69492.2026.11505080},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041328483?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Srm Valliammai Engineering College, Dept. Of Ece, Tamil Nadu, Kattankulathur, 603 203, India},
	abstract = {The ignition of gas stoves being unattended has been one of the major causes of deaths in residential fires around the globe. In 2017-2021, 158,400 domestic cooking fires took place on average each year in the United States, resulting in the deaths of 470 civilians, injuries to 4,150 people, and property damage costing corporations 1.15 billion dollars [1]. Current commercial offerings rely on naive, timer-driven shutoffs or independent gas detectors that lack situational awareness. In this paper, CookSafe AI, a new edge-AI platform implemented on an ESP32-S3 microcontroller [2] fusing multi-modal sensors, a quantised MobileNetV2 convolutional neural network [3] to classify flame states, an Isolation Forest [4] anomaly detector to detect novel hazard patterns and a closed-loop motorised actuation system to control a gas knob autonomously, is presented. It is a system that combines the output of an MQ-6 LPG gas sensor, an MLX90614 infrared thermopile, an ultrasonic proximity sensor (HC-SR04), a rotary encoder (KY-040), and a camera (OV2640). MobileNetV2, when quantised to INT8 (97.3 KB), achieves 98.6% accuracy for flame detection at 12 fps on-device using TensorFlow Lite for Microcontrollers [5] with ESP-NN acceleration [6]. The isolation forest anomaly module achieves an F1 Score of 0.94 for new hazard patterns. If unsafe conditions are identified, a NEMA-17 stepper motor having a worm-gear coupling may be programmed to rotate the gas knob to OFF in 1.2 seconds. Real-time monitoring and manual override are provided by a Web dashboard based on MQTT/WebSocket. The experimental findings from 2, 4 0 0 controlled trials show that the system-level hazard mitigation rate is 99.58 per cent, the false-positive rate is 0.83 per cent, and the detection-to-actuation latency is 347 ms on average. Together, CookSafe AI is an Intelligent Autonomous Safety Agent in Smart Homes that can sense its surroundings, analyse multimodal evidence, and autonomously take corrective measures. © 2026 IEEE.},
