	abstract = {Progress in modern times brought both rapid growth of smart devices and Internet of Things (IoT) together with simple connection abilities and automation control. Although the fast growth of smart devices and IoT poses essential security problems that involve data breaches together with unauthorized access and hostile cyber attacks. Limited resources among IoT devices present barriers for traditional security systems built around encryption cryptography and firewall defenses because these systems lack sufficient capability to identify threats in real-time. This study determines methods to enhance IoT and smart system security through lightweight deep learning model integration. Low-power optimized neural networks including MobileNet, TinyML and Quantized CNNs enable detection of anomalies together with malware signs and instant threat response utilizing minimum energy consumption compared to conventional deep learning systems that demand substantial processing resources. The proposed solution provides automated adaptation of security measures through federated learning and edge AI as well as adversarial defenses for privacy protection. Research demonstrates that low-cost processing supports lightweight deep learning models which achieve high accuracy levels exceeding 95% thus making them suitable for securing industrial automation systems as well as healthcare wearable's smart homes and IoT networks. Deep learning models that operate efficiently enable IoT devices to deliver automatic real-time protection against cyber attacks which results in higher privacy standards as well as dependability and resilience in smart environments of the future. © 2025 IEEE.},
