	abstract = {Cloud-dependent anomaly detection in industrial Internet of Things (IoT) introduces prohibitive latency, bandwidth costs, and data privacy risks for real-time predictive maintenance. To overcome this, we present WhisperNet, a novel TinyML architecture for direct deployment on resource-constrained microcontroller units (MCUs). WhisperNet employs a hybrid 1D-CNN and Depthwise Separable Convolution design, enhanced with a temporal attention module to efficiently extract salient features from vibration signals. The model was optimized via post-training integer quantization for ARM Cortex-M cores. Evaluated on the CWRU bearing dataset, WhisperNet achieves 94.2% F1-score accuracy with an inference time of 25 ms, consumes under 50 mW of power, and requires only 250 KB of memory. This demonstrates a practical, cost-effective, and privacy-preserving solution for on-device, real-time anomaly detection in industrial machinery. © 2026 IEEE.},
