	abstract = {The advent of Industry 4.0 highlights the pressing demand for efficient, real-time anomaly detection in industrial sys-tems. This study introduces a framework that integrates multi-task deep learning with Tiny Machine Learning (tinyML) techniques, specifically designed for conveyor belt systems. By combining time-series signal processing and multi-sensor fusion, the frame-work effectively tackles both regression and multi-classification tasks. It enables real-time monitoring of conveyor states, accurate estimation of pallet weight, and precise determination of pallet position. This approach not only ensures seamless operation but also paves the way for advanced predictive maintenance and enhanced operational efficiency in industrial settings. High-frequency sensor data - capturing vibration, motor current, and belt speed - were leveraged to train deep learning models, including Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP), Convolutional Neural Network (CNN), Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM), and Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) architectures. To address deployment challenges such as hardware limitations, operating system compati-bility, and real-time constraints, the models used were optimized for TinyML and edge devices. Experimental results validate the framework's scalability and performance, with LSTM achieving 99% classification accuracy and a 25% of Focussed Indicator of Precision and Recall Balance (F1-score) for 8-class tasks, alongside 90% accuracy for regression tasks running on desktop system. Notably, CNN models optimized, quantized and converted to TinyML demonstrated superior performance on the STM32 Micro-controller (MCU). These findings establish the proposed framework as a practical solution for real-time monitoring and predictive maintenance in industrial environments. © 2026 Author(s).},
