	abstract = {TinyML, FL, and cutting-edge deep learning for resource-efficient anomaly identification in agriculture and industry which combines and we created the an Enhanced TinyML Framework with Deep FL Supported Real- Time Anomaly Detection in an IoT Environment (ETDFAD) model. Starting with the preparation of datasets, images of chicken eggs were standardized to enhance robustness for practical use. U sing the lightweight 'TensorFlores' framework, the model maximizes deployment on resource-limited hardware such the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense focusing on training and optimized power consumption, ensuring long runtime in remote environments. A customized Federated Averaging (F edA vg) algorithm accounts for device diversity and minimizes slower node impact, ensuring project scalability. The ETDFAD also allows for specific anomaly detection in metallurgical facilities using a GLMS and Bidirectional LSTM integration, effectively capturing dependencies in vibration data. The following parameters are used such as training and validation accuracy and loss, precision-recall curve, ROC Curve and its performance is calculated. © 2025 IEEE.},
